; maps surface words to graph concepts: λ: Word → Node ∪ {⊥}
; word-node "heavier" → viveka-max
; shabda-anveshana "birds" → bird
; includes stemming (birds→bird) and alias resolution (heavier→viveka-max).
; returns ⊥ (mithya) when the word is unknown.
; 
; this is the boundary between language and graph.
; used 20 times across tantras (word-node + shabda-anveshana).
; pure: same word always resolves to same concept.

(kosha lexicon-morphism
  (vishesa computation-varga)
  (swarupa morphism)
  (sthita function domain-computation)
  (janya shabda))
